{"skill":{"slug":"vercel","displayName":"Vercel Platform"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1768364797852,"changelog":"Improved description for clarity","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6755,"sha256":"cea77fbe0275178bdef0373d521a8ec80e7fa957aae7073d88aa451009df47e0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1863,"sha256":"aa466b9c17734069be40ab40ead00e280a1dce2fac7607c22af2be70651f56e3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015629626,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e7dfa9f38edddfdcd4dcf02236f0ac4da8cde4156b955b28dd1da04b2b95230c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e7dfa9f38edddfdcd4dcf02236f0ac4da8cde4156b955b28dd1da04b2b95230c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: vercel\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle provides a comprehensive interface to the Vercel CLI, documenting its commands and options. The `SKILL.md` file contains instructions for fetching Vercel documentation using `curl` from `vercel.com` and lists various `vercel` CLI commands for deployments, project management, environment variables, and domains. All documented actions are legitimate operations for interacting with the Vercel platform and its documentation. There is no evidence of prompt injection attempts, data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation. The skill's behavior is clearly aligned with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159737519},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":61,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789015629626},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward Vercel CLI reference skill, with expected but sensitive deployment, domain, and environment-variable commands that users should run carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using this skill can affect live Vercel projects and can materialize secrets into files such as .env.local, which is proportionate to Vercel administration but requires user care.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file with metadata requiring the existing vercel and curl binaries; no install script, bundled executable, dependency install, or remote code execution path was present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill is broad and includes production deploys, project/domain removal, rollback, promotion, domain purchase/transfer, env-var pulls, and auth-token options, but it presents them as CLI reference material rather than hidden or automatic actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background worker, memory write, tool hijacking, or privilege-escalation mechanism was found; any authentication use depends on normal Vercel CLI login or token handling.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is deploying and managing Vercel applications, projects, domains, environment variables, logs, and documentation; the listed capabilities align with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent to help administer Vercel projects. Before running commands that deploy to production, remove resources, change domains, buy or transfer domains, or pull environment variables, confirm the target project/team/environment and keep secret files like .env.local out of logs and version control.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The env pull examples are normal Vercel environment-management operations; the scanner concern is valid as user guidance because the skill does not warn that pulled env files contain secrets, but the artifact does not hide or exfiltrate credentials.\n[EA2] expected: The --yes and --force options are documented as CLI options, and the artifact does not instruct an agent to use them autonomously or for destructive actions by default.\n[SQP-2] expected: Production-impacting and destructive Vercel commands are purpose-aligned for a complete CLI reference, though the skill would be safer with explicit confirmation and scope-check guidance before remove, rollback, promote, domain, and secret-handling commands.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015629626}}}}}